  "conclusion": "All four sides use all 512 ports at a virtual pitch of 0.175 mm, exactly equal to the required centerline clearance. The first 5 mm band is therefore 100% occupied by mandatory port stubs inside every connector footprint, and no additional parallel lane can be inserted between adjacent ports (0 spare lanes). Spare lanes exist only in the 15 inter-connector gaps of each side. The board is not globally lane-length exhausted; the binding constraints are the saturated boundary/turn bands and corner turn squares, where every route must bend within a 5 mm radius while its neighbours sit exactly one clearance away."
